---
slug: .well-known/oauth-protected-resource
method: get
format: json
---
{%- comment -%}
  OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728, spec §9.5). An MCP client that
  receives a 401 discovers where to obtain a token by reading this document. The
  resource identifier is per-instance (multi-tenancy, §15). authorization_servers
  is advertised only when an issuer is configured.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function cfg = 'modules/mcp/commands/config'
  assign doc = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign doc['resource'] = cfg.resource_identifier
  hash_assign doc['resource_name'] = cfg.server_name
  assign methods = '["header"]' | parse_json
  hash_assign doc['bearer_methods_supported'] = methods
  unless cfg.oauth.issuer == blank
    assign servers = '[]' | parse_json
    assign servers = servers | array_add: cfg.oauth.issuer
    hash_assign doc['authorization_servers'] = servers
  endunless
  response_status 200
  echo doc
-%}
